# PR Review Agent — environment file
#
# Copy this file to .claude/env and fill in the values:
#     cp .claude/env.example .claude/env
#     chmod 600 .claude/env
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - .claude/env MUST NOT be committed to git. The installer adds it to
#   .gitignore. Verify with: grep '^.claude/env$' .gitignore
# - Do not paste secrets into chat with Claude or anywhere else they may
#   end up in logs.
# - Treat this file like ~/.ssh/id_rsa: chmod 600 .claude/env

# ===== FORGEJO_PASSWORD =====
#
# The credential the agent uses to read PRs and post reviews.
#
# >>> STRONGLY RECOMMENDED: use a Personal Access Token (PAT), not a
# >>> password. The variable name is FORGEJO_PASSWORD for compatibility
# >>> with HTTP Basic Auth, but Forgejo accepts a PAT as the password
# >>> value, which works identically for API calls.
#
# Why a PAT, not a password:
# - Many Forgejo instances disable basic-auth-with-password for the API.
#   You'll see "user's password is invalid" even with the right password.
#   PATs are the supported path.
# - PATs can be scoped (read PRs + write reviews, but not delete repos).
# - PATs can be revoked without changing your account password.
# - PATs work even when 2FA is enabled on your account.
# - Failed login attempts on a PAT don't lock your account.
#
# How to mint a PAT:
# 1. Sign in to your Forgejo instance as the reviewer user.
#    (Use a private/incognito window if you're already signed in as
#    someone else and the reviewer account is different.)
# 2. Settings -> Applications -> Manage Access Tokens -> Generate New Token
# 3. Name: "claude-pr-review" or similar
# 4. Scopes: at minimum
#      - read:repository  (list PRs, fetch diffs)
#      - read:issue       (read existing reviews and comments)
#      - write:issue      (post review verdicts and comments)
#    For headroom, just pick "repo" full access.
# 5. Copy the token IMMEDIATELY. Forgejo only shows it once.
# 6. Paste below as the value of FORGEJO_PASSWORD. The variable name
#    stays as-is.
#
# Identity check after setting it:
#   set -a && source .claude/env && set +a
#   curl -s -u "USERNAME:$FORGEJO_PASSWORD" \
#     -H "cf-access-token: $(cloudflared access token --app=BASE_URL)" \
#     BASE_URL/api/v1/user | python3 -m json.tool | head
# Expected: a user object whose `login` field matches the reviewer's username.
# Wrong login = wrong PAT (you generated it as a different user). Forgejo
# rejects self-reviews, so identity matters.

FORGEJO_PASSWORD=

# ===== Cloudflare Access (optional) =====
#
# If your Forgejo instance is behind Cloudflare Access, the agent fetches
# a fresh token via `cloudflared access token --app=<base_url>` on each run.
# Requires a prior interactive login: `cloudflared access login <base_url>`.
#
# If your Forgejo is NOT behind Cloudflare Access, leave CF_ACCESS_REQUIRED
# unset; the agent will skip the cloudflared step.
#
# If it IS behind Cloudflare Access and you want the agent to fail loudly
# when cloudflared isn't available (instead of silently sending
# unauthenticated requests that may bypass intended access controls),
# set this to "1".
# CF_ACCESS_REQUIRED=1
